00:20:47,860 --> 00:20:51,159
And go back to good old lecture 1 and 2,

436
00:20:51,159 --> 00:20:55,120
talking about the word RAM model of computation.

437
00:20:55,120 --> 00:20:58,899
A question here that usually doesn't matter in this class.

438
00:20:58,899 --> 00:21:01,520
Usually we assume additions take constant time.

439
00:21:01,520 --> 00:21:04,540
And we usually do that because it's usually true.

440
00:21:04,540 --> 00:21:09,860
And in general, our model is that w bit additions,

441
00:21:09,860 --> 00:21:13,959
where w is our machine word size, takes constant time.

442
00:21:17,860 --> 00:21:20,840
And that's not the real problem.

443
00:21:20,840 --> 00:21:24,120
But for this problem and this problem only pretty much,

444
00:21:24,120 --> 00:21:27,179
for Fibonacci numbers, I happen to know that the Fibonacci

